cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Australian Raptor CNN + AUSLAN: Deep-learning identification of Australian birds of prey with inclusive sign-language vocabulary"
type: software
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-05-01"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ZOMBIECRAFTIAN/raptor-australia"
abstract: >-
  A convolutional neural network (EfficientNetB4 transfer learning)
  for identifying eight raptor species of southeastern Australia,
  paired with a provisional Australian Sign Language (AUSLAN)
  vocabulary for accessible citizen science. The dataset is sourced
  from iNaturalist Australia and the Atlas of Living Australia.
  Observations can be exported in Darwin Core format for upload to
  the Atlas of Living Australia and other GBIF data publishers.
keywords:
  - "computer vision"
  - "convolutional neural networks"
  - "biodiversity"
  - "raptors"
  - "Australia"
  - "AUSLAN"
  - "deep learning"
  - "transfer learning"
  - "Darwin Core"
authors:
  - family-names: "Fernández Báez"
    given-names: "Brian"
    affiliation: "Instituto Tecnológico de Veracruz, Mexico"
preferred-citation:
